comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-08T05:53:41.780Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status 2658-item title/metadata catalog and source ledger reviewed; current query receiver relative context handoff nearest pm-4k6b,pm-kcs4,pm-3crymx,pm-doxj,pm-vvib. No individual owner for this experiment was found. Shared scorer/signal/packer baselines are prerequisites, not proof of this distinct mechanism. User requested individual planning records; this draft preserves the open cognitive-architecture decision gate and does not accept the ADR. Estimate is a one-day initial spike budget, not a delivery forecast."
body: "## Proposal and provenance\n\nStable algorithm slug: `receiver-relative-context-handoff`. Source: pm-vvib note recorded 2026-07-07T15:12:26.415Z.\n\nCognitive subsystem 5 from pm-vvib. (5) Theory of mind / common ground — humans model what OTHER minds already know and communicate only the delta; effective multi-agent coordination needs the same. pm mapping: every agent's knowledge horizon is already derivable from the immutable episodic streams (the watermark of candidate #4, but computed for ANY author, not just self). Two compositions: (a) handoff briefs — when work moves between agents (claim transfer, review request, plan step reassignment), assemble context relative to the RECEIVER's watermark, so a claim handoff costs only the tokens of what the receiver has not seen; (b) expertise routing — 'who knows about X' answered by episodic-trace density per author over the semantic neighborhood of X (which agent authored/touched the most relevant history), turning authorship provenance into a coordination primitive for workspaces with thousands of concurrent agents. Zero new stored state — pure derivation from history streams plus the hybrid index. Distinct from #4 novelty detection (self-directed catching-up) and from pm-4k6b author affinity (ranking MY items); this is other-directed: minimizing what must be transmitted between minds. Small-workspace neutral: single-author workspaces derive an empty delta and the subsystem is silent.\n\n## Delivery boundary\n\nEvaluate this mechanism as a bounded public-SDK experiment before any production adoption. Use the existing scorer and packer contracts; no CLI-only behavior or new command noun. The historical catalog is design input, not evidence that this mechanism was implemented.\n\n## Experiment protocol\n\nFreeze a workspace/history revision and parameter manifest. Compare against the current deterministic SDK baseline using held-out judgments and negative controls. Report nDCG/action success, critical-evidence omission, latency p50/p95, peak memory, tokens per completed task, and rebuild cost separately. Include 3-item/minutes, real-shaped, 100k/1M-item, decades-long, and sparse/dense/imbalanced graph scenarios; smoke subsets may not claim scale acceptance. Bound candidate counts, graph expansions, elapsed time, and output size, with cancellation and completeness receipts. Record exact versus approximate behavior and approximation error; theoretical guarantees require their stated assumptions. Missing or untrusted evidence remains unknown, never inferred proof.\n\nPromotion requires a reproducible quality improvement on the held-out target population, no regression of existing exact invariants or mandatory gates, and a declared compute/token cost justified by that improvement. Reject or defer with the same immutable evidence if those conditions fail. No production default, adaptive learning, or data export is authorized by this planning item."
